---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Data With Duke">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20">
    <header class="mb-16 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-black text-blue-900 mb-6">About the Project</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Data isn't just for spreadsheets and algorithms. It's the story of our lives.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-slate lg:prose-xl max-w-none 
                prose-headings:text-blue-900 prose-headings:font-bold
                prose-p:leading-relaxed">
      
      <h2>Why "Data With Duke"?</h2>
      <p>
        The goal here is simple: to bridge the gap between technical data engineering 
        and everyday decision-making. I believe that data literacy is a fundamental 
        skill for the 21st century.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        "Helping you take ownership of the data that impacts your life."
      </blockquote>

      <h2>What we cover</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Critical Thinking:</strong> How to spot bad statistics in the wild.</li>
        <li><strong>Tool Mastery:</strong> From Excel basics to Python automation.</li>
        <li><strong>Data Ethics:</strong> Privacy, AI transparency, and the internet of things.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="mt-12 p-8 bg-blue-50 rounded-3xl border border-blue-100">
        <h3 class="mt-0">AI Transparency</h3>
        <p class="mb-0">
          We practice what we preach. For more on how we use technology to build this site, 
          check out our <a href="/transparency">AI Transparency Statement</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>